---
title: ROOT KEYS
--- 
%% Made in Mermaid (https://mermaid.live)
%% DESCRIPTION: This diagram shows how all the root keys are computed and stored. The lower-hierarchy keys and data are not shown here - they have separate diagrams.
%% DIAGRAM SUMMARY: A password-derived Master Key is used to decrypt and verify the server-stored client state, which includes 2 root keys: Root DEK (Data Encryption Key) and Root IK (Identity Key).

%% SHAPES:
%% - Rectangles mean operations/algorithms
%% - Rounded rectangles mean data
%% - Dashed borders mean that the diagram ends there, but the logic does not and more detailed info can be found elsewhere
%% - Parallelograms mean user input from UI
%% COLORS:
%% - Red means the most-confidential secrets that are never stored persistently in plaintexts, and should only be computed by the client when really needed (which isn't needed often). A compromise means that the account cannot be secured anymore and should be completely deleted and re-created.
%% - Orange means secrets that still allow access to the account's private data, however, security of the FUTURE data can still be restored by choosing new keys if the current ones leak (assuming nothing "red" was leaked). "Orange" secrets might need to be stored persistently to allow access.

flowchart TB
    classDef red color:#f00,stroke:#f00
    classDef orange color:#f60,stroke:#f60
    classDef dashed stroke-dasharray: 5 5

    subgraph SERVER
        %% SERVER STORAGE
        encState(["Encrypted and authenticated client state"])
        userAccount([Non-secret user account data])
    end

    %% SERVER-CLIENT TRANSFERS
    userAccount -->|login| login
    encState -->|payload| stateAead


    subgraph CLIENT
        %% PASSWORD KEY DERIVIATION
        login[/"User login (from UI or from server if user logged in via email/phone)"/] -->|salt| passDeriv["`Key derivation (argon2id)`"]
        pass[/USER PASSWORD/] -->|payload| passDeriv
        passDeriv --> mk(["Master Key (MK)"])
        mk -->|key| stateAead["Decryption and verification (AEAD)"]
        stateAead --> state(["Decrypted state, including version number and root keys (see: Replay Protection)"])
        class pass,mk red
        class state dashed

        %% IDENTITY KEYS
        state --> wrappedRootIkPriv(["MK-Wrapped Root Identity Key priv (see: Identity Keys)"])
        wrappedRootIkPriv -->|unwrap with MK| rootIkPriv(["Root Identity Key private"])
        class wrappedRootIkPriv,rootIkPriv dashed
        class rootIkPriv red

        %% DATA
        state --> rootDk(["Root Data Key (Root DK)"])
        state --> operationalIks(["Operational Identity Keys (OIKs; pub+priv)"])
        class rootDk,operationalIks orange
    end

